"surface":"பலவே","parts":[{"text":"பல","lemma":"பல","gloss":"many"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ஏ","gloss":"emphatic"}],"gloss":"many indeed"}]}],"literal":"As the morning star appeared and bird calls sounded, / at early dawn, praising many oxen, / even if appearing at his gate, he does not go to another's gate; / hearing the sound of the wide-surfaced taṭāri drum and showing grace, / desiring that my poverty be removed, / removing the rags worn away by the ground and torn from my waist, / clothing me in white cloth, he removed my hunger. / The lord of Ambar with paddy-growing fields and fertile gardens reached by the Kaveri river, / good Aruvantai, may he live long! / May his days be even more than the raindrops falling / on the strong mountain of dense Vengadam / from the lofty sky!","translation":"As the morning star rises and birds begin to chirp, at the break of dawn, the plowmen praise their many oxen. Even if one stands at his gate, he never goes seeking another's gate. Hearing the sound of my wide-headed taṭāri drum, he showed grace. Desiring to banish my poverty, he stripped away the dirty, earth-worn rags from my waist, clothed me in clean white garments, and drove away my hunger. He is Aruvantai, the good lord of Ambar, where the Kaveri river embraces fertile gardens and paddy-growing fields. May he live long! May his days be more numerous than the raindrops that fall from the lofty sky onto the strong, forest-clad peaks of Mount Vengadam!","modern":"விடிவெள்ளி தோன்றப் பறவைகள் ஒலிக்கத் தொடங்கும் அதிகாலைப் பொழுதில், உழவர்கள் தங்கள் எருதுகளைப் போற்றிப் புகழ்கின்றனர். இரவலர்கள் அவனது வாயிலில் நின்றாலும், அவன் பிறருடைய வாயிலை நாடிச் செல்லாத பெருமிதம் உடையவன். எனது அகன்ற வாயைக் கொண்ட தடாரிப் பறையின் இசையைக் கேட்டு இரங்கி, எனது வறுமை நீங்க வேண்டும் என்று விரும்பி, எனது இடையில் இருந்த, மண்ணில் பட்டுத் தேய்ந்து கிழிந்த கந்தல் துணிகளைக் களைந்து, தூய வெண்ணிற ஆடையை உடுத்தி, எனது பசியைப் போக்கினான். காவிரி ஆறு பாயும் சோலைகளையும், நெல் விளையும் கழனிகளையும் கொண்ட அம்பர் என்னும் ஊரின் தலைவனான நல்ல அருவந்தை என்பவன் பல்லாண்டு வாழ்க! உயர்ந்த வானத்திலிருந்து, அடர்ந்த காடுகளைக் கொண்ட வலிமையான வேங்கட மலையின் மேல் விழும் மழைத்துளிகளைக் காட்டிலும் அவனது வாழ்நாள் பலவாக நீடிப்பதாக!","explanation":"The poet Kallāṭaṉār sings in praise of his patron, Ampar Kiḻāṉ Aruvantai, a generous chieftain of the fertile Ambar region. The poem opens with a vivid description of dawn, when birds chirp and farmers praise their oxen, setting a tone of morning renewal. The poet highlights Aruvantai's unique nobility: while suppliants crowd his gate, he himself never has to beg at anyone else's gate. Hearing the poet's drum, Aruvantai immediately replaces his dirty, earth-worn rags with clean white clothes and feeds him. The transition from the dark, dirty rags to the bright white cloth symbolizes the transformation of the poet's life from bleak poverty to prosperous comfort. The blessing at the end compares the patron's lifespan to the countless raindrops falling on the sacred Vengadam hills, wishing him a long and glorious life.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"},"timing":{"male":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.8],[0.88,1.5],[1.5,1.7],[1.7,2.8],[2.8,3.0],[3.0,3.7],[3.7,3.7],[3.7,3.7],[3.7,5.6],[5.6,6.0],[6.0,6.5],[6.5,6.8],[6.8,6.8],[6.8,6.8],[6.8,8.9],[8.9,9.2],[9.2,9.4],[9.6,10.6],[10.6,10.7],[10.7,11.1],[11.1,11.2],[11.2,12.4],[12.4,12.9],[12.9,13.1],[13.35,13.5],[13.7,14.7],[14.7,14.7],[14.7,15.3],[15.3,15.5],[15.7,16.1],[16.1,17.0],[17.0,17.2],[17.2,17.2],[17.2,17.5],[18.88,19.58],[19.58,19.98],[19.98,20.18],[20.18,20.58],[20.58,21.48],[21.48,21.78],[21.78,21.98],[21.98,22.28],[22.28,23.68],[23.68,24.18],[24.18,24.48],[24.48,25.08],[25.08,25.38],[25.38,25.58],[25.58,25.98]],"female":[[0.0,0.5],[0.5,0.8],[0.95,1.7],[1.7,2.0],[2.0,3.3],[3.3,3.4],[3.4,4.2],[4.2,4.2],[4.2,4.2],[4.2,6.4],[6.4,6.7],[6.7,7.1],[7.1,7.4],[7.4,8.74],[8.74,8.74],[8.74,10.0],[10.0,10.3],[10.3,10.6],[10.9,11.8],[11.8,12.2],[12.2,12.5],[12.5,12.5],[12.5,12.8],[12.8,13.1],[13.1,13.4],[13.4,13.7],[13.7,14.0],[14.0,14.3],[14.3,14.6],[14.6,14.9],[14.9,15.2],[15.2,15.5],[15.5,15.8],[15.8,16.1],[16.1,16.4],[21.2,21.9],[21.9,22.4],[22.4,22.7],[22.7,23.1],[23.1,24.0],[24.0,24.3],[24.3,24.6],[24.6,24.9],[24.9,26.4],[26.4,26.4],[26.4,26.4],[26.4,27.8],[27.8,28.3],[28.3,28.5],[28.5,29.0]]},"sync":[[["வெள்ளி","morning star"]],[["தோன்ற","as it appeared"]],[["புள்ளுக்குரல்","bird calls"]],[["இயம்ப","to sound"]],[["புலரி","dawn"]],[["விடியல்","early morning"]],[["பகடுபல","many oxen"]],[["வாழ்த்தி","praising"]],[["தன்கடை","his gate"]],[["தோன்றினும்","even if appearing"]],[["இலனே","he does not go"]],[["பிறன்கடை","other's gate"]],[["பிறன்கடை","other's gate"]],[["அகன்கண்","wide-surfaced"]],[["தடாரி","taṭāri drum"]],[["பாடுகேட்டு","having heard the sound"]],[["அருளி","having shown grace"]],[["வறன்","poverty"],["யான்","I"]],[["நீங்கல்","to be removed"]],[["வேண்டி","desiring"]],[["என்","my"]],[["அரை","waist"]],[["நிலந்தின","worn away by the ground"]],[["சிதைந்த","torn"]],[["சிதாஅர்","rags"]],[["களைந்து","having removed"]],[["வெளியது","white cloth"]],[["உடீஇ","having clothed me with"]],[["என்","my"]],[["பசிகளைந்தோனே","he who removed my hunger"]],[["பசிகளைந்தோனே","he who removed my hunger"]],[["காவிரி","Kaveri river"]],[["அணையும்","which reaches"]],[["தாழ்நீர்","deep water"],["படப்பை","fertile gardens"]],[["படப்பை","fertile gardens"]],[["நெல்விளை","paddy-growing"]],[["கழனி","fields"]],[["அம்பர்","of Ambar"]],[["கிழவோன்","the lord"]],[["நல்அருவந்தை","good Aruvantai"]],[["நல்அருவந்தை","good Aruvantai"]],[["வாழியர்","may he live long"]],[["புல்லிய","dense"]],[["வேங்கட","Vengadam"]],[["விறல்வரை","strong mountain"],["பட்ட","falling"]],[["பட்ட","falling"]],[["ஓங்கல்","lofty"]],[["வானத்து","of the sky"]],[["உறையினும்","even more than the raindrops"]],[["பலவே","many indeed"]]]}